.TH geectl-build-build-history 1  "geectl-build-build-history 0.2.2" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-build\-build\-history \- List the completed builds for a package, newest first
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl build build\-history\fR [\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> <\fIPACKAGE\fR> <\fIREPOSITORY\fR> <\fIARCH\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
List the completed builds for a package, newest first
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR
At most this many entries
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project the package is in
.TP
<\fIPACKAGE\fR>
The package to list the history for
.TP
<\fIREPOSITORY\fR>
The repository the package builds in
.TP
<\fIARCH\fR>
The architecture the package builds for
.SH VERSION
v0.2.2
